      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes requested** — See inline comments for details. [[trajectory](go/traj/6e454b68-5018-4fb8-9815-48525c66dc08)]\n\n### Review Summary\n\n*   **Functionality:** The transition to `select.select()` successfully eliminates the need for background threads. However, there are two related edge cases that will cause the test script to incorrectly throw an EOF or block indefinitely: `io.RawIOBase.read()` returning `None` instead of throwing `BlockingIOError`, and sockets/PTYs being blocking by default which leaves them susceptible to spurious wakeups. See inline comments.\n*   **Style:** The code refactoring is very clean, especially leveraging the walrus operator.\n*   **Security:** No security issues identified.\n*   **Testing:** Manual testing is appropriate for this orchestrator script, but the edge cases identified above should be addressed to ensure test stability in CI environments.\n*   **CL Size \u0026 Scope:** The CL size is perfect and tightly scoped to replacing the ThreadPoolExecutor.",
