      "side": 1,
      "message": "When `file` is in non-blocking mode (which it must be to truly prevent blocking—see my other comment), Python\u0027s `io.RawIOBase.read()` returns `None` when no bytes are available (the equivalent of `EAGAIN`) instead of raising a `BlockingIOError`.\n\nCurrently, if `ch` is `None`, `if not ch:` evaluates to `True`, which incorrectly treats the non-blocking read as an `EOFError` or an end-of-line. Additionally, if the code were to reach the next line, `line.extend(None)` would crash with a `TypeError`.\n\nTo fix this, explicitly check if `ch is None` and `continue` to the next iteration:\n\n```python\n        try:\n            ch \u003d file.read(1)\n        except OSError as e:\n            if e.errno in (errno.EAGAIN, errno.EWOULDBLOCK):\n                continue\n            ch \u003d b\"\"\n\n        if ch is None:\n            continue\n\n        if not ch:\n            if not line:\n                raise EOFError(\"Console disconnected\")\n            break\n```",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "939b2e168cf09514d67d8d274d37d87ea010b620",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
